- **Paired at 24K**, against the full cache's
  {{ phase17.analysis.quality.summary.full_24576.mean | pct }} on the same prompts, the tier keeps
  {{ phase17.analysis.quality.summary.retention_24576_b1250.value | pct }} ({{ phase17.analysis.quality.summary.retention_24576_b1250.lo | pct }}–{{ phase17.analysis.quality.summary.retention_24576_b1250.hi | pct }})
  of its score at 12.5% and
  {{ phase17.analysis.quality.summary.retention_24576_b625.value | pct }} ({{ phase17.analysis.quality.summary.retention_24576_b625.lo | pct }}–{{ phase17.analysis.quality.summary.retention_24576_b625.hi | pct }})
  at 6.25%. Tiered prefill is bit-identical to the full-cache path, so these are rung 6's own
  retentions at 24K.
- **How quality moves with context at a fixed budget fraction is not resolved.** From 16K to 64K
  the tier's score goes from {{ phase17.analysis.quality.summary.tiered_16384_b1250.mean | pct }} to {{ phase17.analysis.quality.summary.tiered_65536_b1250.mean | pct }}
  at 12.5% and from {{ phase17.analysis.quality.summary.tiered_16384_b625.mean | pct }} to {{ phase17.analysis.quality.summary.tiered_65536_b625.mean | pct }} at
  6.25%: in opposite directions, with overlapping CIs at 45 prompts per cell. A fixed fraction is
  four times as many blocks at 64K as at 16K, while a needle is still about one block, so there is
  no reason to expect the fraction alone to set quality; this data cannot say more.
- **The quality kernel costs more memory and time than the capacity run's.** The 64K prefill took
  {{ phase17.analysis.quality.summary.tiered_65536_b1250.prefill_s_median | .1f }} s (median) against
  {{ phase17.analysis.capacity.models.3b.tiered_max_prefill_s | .1f }} s on cuDNN, with the allocator
  hitting its cap and flushing repeatedly. Capacity under the quality kernel was not swept.

## What this phase does not show

- Two models, one prompt per capacity cell, one run per cell: the capacity table answers "does it
  run", and its timings are single measurements.
- The tier's own limits were not found: the 1B ladder stops at the model's context window and the
  3B ladder at 64K, chosen to keep the host store well inside 16 GB of RAM.
- No host tier below RAM (no SSD), so host RAM is the bound on context.

